  "question": "Given $$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad C=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix},$$ verify that $(A+B)+C=A+(B+C)$.",
  "answeroption": "C",
  "explanation": "<b>Evaluation of $(A+B)+C$</b><br>$$A+B=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$$<br>Therefore, $$(A+B)+C=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$$<br><b>Evaluation of $A+(B+C)$</b><br>$$B+C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$$<br>Hence, $$A+(B+C)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$$<br><b>Associative property</b><br>Thus, $(A+B)+C=A+(B+C)$.",
